From f9252c7dbbc46d4a063ce38b1c3f2f066dea788b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 08:00:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dues): add Undo for a wrongly-recorded payment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There was no way to reverse a wrongly-recorded Dues payment short of a
manual database fix. Adds an Undo action per payment in Bills &
Payments:

- Backend: POST /dues/payments/:id/undo (Treasurer/Manager only).
  Cancels the payment's journal entry (status -> CANCELLED, with who
  and why) rather than deleting it — every report already only reads
  POSTED entries, so this alone drops it from Cash Book, Day Book,
  Ledger, Trial Balance, P&L and Balance Sheet while keeping an audit
  trail. If a resident's UPI claim pointed at this payment, it's
  detached and reset to PENDING for proper re-review instead of being
  silently lost. The Payment row is deleted and the bill's status is
  recomputed from what's left (Unpaid/Partial/Paid; a Waived bill is
  left alone). Blocked for Razorpay gateway payments — real money
  already settled there, so undoing here would misstate the books
  without refunding anyone — and for entries in a closed financial
  year, and for a payment already undone.
- Frontend: bill rows with any payment history (not just payable
  ones) now open a panel showing each payment with an Undo button
  (a lock icon instead, for Razorpay ones) and an inline confirm
  step before it fires.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
